# The value a merge binds is the value its name has where the merge
# stands. wrap declares a field named like its formal, 7, and returns
# merge(add; y: k): the node binds 7, whatever wrap was called with.
# wrap 5 and wrap 100 each give 7 + 1. The merge is written with the model
# first; the bound formal is left at its default: a bounded case
# (steps/defects.md, MERGE-KEEPS-MODEL-INTERFACE). Entry 7.
fn: add (int: y; int: x) int
    return: y + x

fn: wrap (int: k) fn: (int: x) int
    int: k 7
    return: merge(add; y: k)

w: wrap 5
u: wrap 100
int: a (w: 1)
int: b (u: 1)
int: ok 7
if: a != 8 || b != 8
    ok: 81
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
